Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:08.48,Default,,0,0,800,,{\b1\4c&H0000FF&\fs40}LAUGHING MAN FANSUBS{\b0}
Dialogue: 0,0:00:08.69,0:00:11.19,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,I'm a soldier - that means I'm
Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.39,0:00:14.59,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,Both a defendant and the judge
Dialogue: 0,0:00:15.39,0:00:19.99,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,I am standing on both ends of the flame
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.67,0:00:24.77,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,Rounding curves
Dialogue: 0,0:00:24.97,0:00:27.67,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,Overtaking life and death,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.67,0:00:33.57,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,I run and fight with false shadows
Dialogue: 0,0:00:33.87,0:00:40.17,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,No matter how many threads of\Ndeception are woven together,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.57,0:00:48.07,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,The truth shall illuminate\Nthe face of light
Dialogue: 0,0:00:49.07,0:00:51.87,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,Save your tears for the day
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.17,0:00:55.17,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,When our pain is far behind
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.57,0:00:58.67,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,On your feet, come with me
Dialogue: 0,0:00:58.47,0:01:01.67,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,We are soldiers stand or die
Dialogue: 0,0:01:01.97,0:01:04.87,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,Save your fears, take your place
Dialogue: 0,0:01:05.07,0:01:08.07,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,Save them for the judgement day
Dialogue: 0,0:01:08.37,0:01:11.27,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,Fast and free, follow me
Dialogue: 0,0:01:11.57,0:01:16.57,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,Time to make the sacrifice.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:16.77,0:01:22.37,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,We rise or fall
Dialogue: 0,0:01:34.97,0:01:37.17,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,That concludes the report
Dialogue: 0,0:01:37.27,0:01:41.17,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,of the SDF members who were involved in the\Nbomb disposal operation at Kyushu Radio Tower.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:42.07,0:01:44.07,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Does this decide matters?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:47.17,0:01:50.53,Sign,,125,0,780,,{\b1\fs40\c&H0000FF&}Kayabuki{\b0}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:44.77,0:01:49.07,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,There are still over ten kilograms\Nof plutonium on Dejima, after all.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:50.97,0:01:51.77,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Prime Minister.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:52.57,0:01:56.77,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,We will announce the deployment\Nof the SDF with that outline.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:56.87,0:01:57.97,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Any objections?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:58.77,0:02:00.97,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,If it is the consensus of the Cabinet,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:01.77,0:02:03.27,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I have no objections.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:06.89,0:02:11.35,Sign - Copy,,500,0,500,,{\b1\i0}The Day the \N Bridge Falls{\b0\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:16.44,0:02:20.14,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,That Cabinet meeting was somewhat\Nforced, wasn't it?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:22.34,0:02:23.94,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Are we going to ignore the statement from China,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:24.04,0:02:29.24,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,and other neighbouring Asian countries,\Nthat we should avoid exercising military force?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:30.01,0:02:32.71,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Countries that have rejected the refugees
Dialogue: 0,0:02:32.81,0:02:35.11,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,have no right to meddle in this affair,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:35.61,0:02:40.81,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,However, our neighbouring countries concerns over\Nmilitary expansion have become even more pronounced...
Dialogue: 0,0:02:39.81,0:02:41.01,Sign,,0,0,250,,That reminds me...
Dialogue: 0,0:02:41.11,0:02:44.31,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,the American Empire has contacted us.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:44.41,0:02:46.61,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,They believe we must not set a precedent
Dialogue: 0,0:02:46.71,0:02:50.91,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,by allowing the refugees to gain autonomy\Nthrough the use of nuclear weapons,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:51.01,0:02:54.21,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,and that we must form a united\Nfront in dealing with this issue,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:54.31,0:02:57.31,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,even if it means we must\Naccelerate the Security Pact.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:57.41,0:02:59.61,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,When was this?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:59.71,0:03:01.11,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I have heard nothing...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:01.21,0:03:04.51,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,They don't trust you,\Nsince they view you as pro-China.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:05.71,0:03:10.01,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,It seems the Kayabuki Cabinet\Nwill only last until Dejima falls.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:29.49,0:03:32.89,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,It's about time for that asshole to notice.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:32.99,0:03:33.99,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:43.52,0:03:48.02,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,We've found the vehicle abandoned at a\Nrest stop on the Nagasaki Expressway.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:48.72,0:03:50.22,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,What about the plutonium?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:50.32,0:03:52.02,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,It hasn't been found.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:52.62,0:03:54.02,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:54.12,0:03:55.42,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,We have no choice.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:56.22,0:03:58.92,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,We can't have the media getting wind of this.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:59.72,0:04:01.72,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,We'd like you to prioritise\Ninformation manipulation
Dialogue: 0,0:04:01.82,0:04:06.52,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,and follow our instructions\Nin retrieving the plutonium.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:06.62,0:04:07.92,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I understand that.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:08.02,0:04:09.32,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I will leave this to you, but...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:09.42,0:04:10.62,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Don't worry.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:10.72,0:04:13.52,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,There will be no problems if\Nyou follow my instructions.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:17.20,0:04:21.30,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I will now return to HQ and adjust the situation.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:21.40,0:04:22.40,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Understood.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:29.00,0:04:33.50,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The Major and the others\Nare on their way to Spring-8
Dialogue: 0,0:04:33.60,0:04:34.70,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:36.91,0:04:40.11,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The SDF deployment has become official.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:40.71,0:04:43.37,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The deployment will begin simultaneously
Dialogue: 0,0:04:43.41,0:04:46.41,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,with the Chief Cabinet Secretary's\Nannouncement at the seven o'clock press conference.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:47.11,0:04:49.51,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,That's in less than an hour.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:49.61,0:04:52.21,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,They will already be on the\Nmove at the Dejima site.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:53.31,0:04:54.61,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Aramaki-San,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:54.71,0:04:58.81,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I don't understand the reason why\Nthe Chief Cabinet Secretary
Dialogue: 0,0:04:58.91,0:05:00.41,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,allowed the situation to deteriorate this far.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:01.21,0:05:03.61,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,This will only lead to an irresolvable conflict.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:04.41,0:05:07.61,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Once war begins, Dejima will fall soon enough,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:07.71,0:05:11.01,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,so it cannot become a hypothetical enemy\Nafter the security pact is renewed.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:11.11,0:05:16.11,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,If so, I don't think it coincides with\Nthe Chief Cabinet Secretary's aim
Dialogue: 0,0:05:16.21,0:05:18.21,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,to establish a military-industrial complex...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:18.31,0:05:19.71,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,That is true,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:19.81,0:05:22.71,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,However, if creating a\Nproblem itself was the goal,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:22.81,0:05:24.61,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,then it makes sense to a certain extent.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:25.21,0:05:27.21,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Even if the refugees surrender,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:27.31,0:05:29.51,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,it is not as though they\Nwill go away and disappear.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:30.51,0:05:35.31,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,We can presume the funds that had been going to maintain the\Nrefugee policy will consequently go to military armaments.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:36.11,0:05:37.81,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Well, yes,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:38.51,0:05:41.61,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,but pressure from China will increase...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:42.61,0:05:46.61,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,It seems there are more factors\Ninvolved than we know of.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:47.61,0:05:48.81,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,How about this, Prime Minister?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:49.81,0:05:54.71,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Why don't we defer the decision to the UN,\Nin order to buy as much time as possible?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:59.90,0:06:01.20,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Major.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:01.30,0:06:04.30,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,There's a GSDF checkpoint ahead.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:05.90,0:06:09.80,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I didn't think they'd let us go that easily,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:09.90,0:06:10.97,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,What's the plan?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:12.10,0:06:14.50,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Major, it's me.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:14.60,0:06:18.90,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Prime Minister Kayabuki just\Nrequested a UN nuclear inspection.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:19.00,0:06:22.60,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,if all goes well, the inspection\Nteam will arrive in two days,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:22.70,0:06:25.90,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,If we can hand over the plutonium then,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:26.00,0:06:29.30,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,there is a good chance that\Nthis situation will blow over,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:29.40,0:06:31.00,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Can you hold out until then?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:31.80,0:06:34.50,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,If we go into hiding somewhere, yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:34.60,0:06:38.20,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I think it'll be extremely difficult\Nto meet the inspection team, however.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:38.30,0:06:40.30,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Figure it out.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:40.40,0:06:43.70,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,This may be the last card left to us.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:45.10,0:06:47.10,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I'll try.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:47.20,0:06:52.10,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Make sure the rookies that stayed\Nbehind at HQ stay out of this,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:52.20,0:06:54.60,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,in case something happens.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:54.70,0:06:57.30,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,We'll do everything on our own from here on.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:57.40,0:06:58.80,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Understood.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:58.90,0:07:00.60,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I'll make the necessary arrangements.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:00.70,0:07:03.50,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Also, about the Tachikoma units...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:05.50,0:07:06.30,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,What's wrong?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:07.00,0:07:08.70,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The comm link was broken.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:09.40,0:07:13.60,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Might be local restriction on communication\Nsystems due to crisis legislation.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:15.70,0:07:17.40,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,It's almost time.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:18.30,0:07:19.80,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I'll go to the press conference room.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:26.76,0:07:29.96,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Will a war break out?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:35.14,0:07:36.84,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The UN...?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:36.94,0:07:38.44,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Did Kayabuki call for them?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:38.54,0:07:39.54,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:43.60,0:07:46.30,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Make preparations to oust her.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:46.40,0:07:47.10,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Understood.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:49.60,0:07:51.10,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Let us begin the press conference.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:40.23,0:08:42.43,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,{\i1}With the SDF's lock-down of Dejima,{\i}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:41.83,0:08:44.75,Sign,,0,200,850,,{\fs52}{\i1\b1}Refugees Declare Independence \N Using Nuclear Deterrence{\i0\b0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:42.53,0:08:45.23,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,{\i1}large-scale traffic regulations have\Nbeen set in place in neighbouring areas.{\i}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:52.93,0:08:58.73,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Today, we will seize our\Nindependence with our own hands!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:17.41,0:09:19.41,Sign,,0,1345,775,,{\fs52}{\b1}LIVE{\b0}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:18.55,0:09:20.35,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,We demand
Dialogue: 0,0:09:23.37,0:09:28.45,Sign,,1275,0,675,,{\fs52}{\u1\b1}LIVE{\u0} \N Nagasaki - Dejima{\b0}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:20.45,0:09:23.95,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,that the Japanese government recognise\NDejima as an independent nation!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:24.05,0:09:26.85,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Then, we can trade freely
Dialogue: 0,0:09:26.95,0:09:28.35,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,and live on our own!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:29.05,0:09:31.25,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,What's wrong with that?!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:31.35,0:09:32.75,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,We have plutonium!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:33.45,0:09:36.35,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The Japanese government has admitted that fact!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:36.45,0:09:38.95,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,This is thanks to Comrade Kuze's efforts!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:39.65,0:09:42.65,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,We'll be forever grateful to\Nhim, and we'll never give him up!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:43.35,0:09:46.55,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Furthermore, the deadline\Nfor attack is in two days.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:46.65,0:09:50.05,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,We will set the UN nuclear inspection team's\Narrival as the final chance for response;
Dialogue: 0,0:09:50.65,0:09:54.15,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,should the refugees not respond by that time,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:54.25,0:09:57.65,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,the preliminary attack will then begin.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:59.25,0:10:00.55,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,That is all.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:03.44,0:10:04.14,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,So it begins.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:05.34,0:10:07.74,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Now that the Chief has been cut off,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:07.74,0:10:11.14,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,we have no choice but to make our own decisions.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:11.94,0:10:17.04,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Whether or not each of you goes\Nany further with this is up to you.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:17.14,0:10:17.94,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Hey!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:18.64,0:10:22.34,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Section 9 didn't form yesterday,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:22.94,0:10:26.24,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Aren't we going to pull a\Nrunning campaign against the SDF?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:26.34,0:10:27.14,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,No.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:27.24,0:10:29.94,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,We're going to take the plutonium to Dejima.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:30.54,0:10:31.84,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Dejima?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:31.94,0:10:32.94,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,That's right.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:32.94,0:10:34.44,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,We'll take advantage of the SDF's advance
Dialogue: 0,0:10:34.54,0:10:36.94,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,and plunge into Dejima.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:37.54,0:10:39.94,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Either way, the inspection\Nteam will come to Dejima.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:40.44,0:10:41.44,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Since that's the case,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:41.54,0:10:44.54,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,we'll catch Kuze before then and hand him over,\Ntogether with the plutonium, in a neat package.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:46.54,0:10:48.94,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,That's ridiculous, but very typical of you.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:49.04,0:10:50.24,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I'm coming.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:51.34,0:10:52.74,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I don't mind, either.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:53.34,0:10:54.81,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Me neither, of course.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:56.04,0:10:58.04,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I also have no objections, but...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:58.94,0:11:00.04,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Are you against it?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:00.94,0:11:01.94,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,No.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:02.44,0:11:05.94,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I'll earn my keep in return for some thrills.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:08.27,0:11:09.67,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,It's decided, then.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:09.77,0:11:13.27,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,{\i1}Major restrictions on traffic were set by\Narmed forces in the city of Nagasaki...{\i}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:09.81,0:11:13.35,Sign,,0,1100,875,,{\fs35}{\b1}Special News Report{\b0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:09.81,0:11:13.35,Sign,,0,750,575,,{\fs35}{\b1}Nagasaki Under Martial Law{\b0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:09.81,0:11:13.35,Sign,,0,700,380,,{\fs35}{\b1}SDF Troops Deployed{\b1}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:13.37,0:11:15.51,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,{\i1}and all domestic flights were...{\i}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:13.36,0:11:15.85,Sign,,0,0,75,,{\b1}Domestic Flights Temporarily Suspended{\b0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:15.86,0:11:18.60,Sign,,0,0,750,,{\b1}Nagasaki Under Martial Law{\b0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:15.87,0:11:18.47,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,{\i1}In such terms,\Nthe decision of the government to...{\i}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:22.48,0:11:24.48,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,How are you doing, Ishikawa?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:24.58,0:11:26.48,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Oh, it's you, Major.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:26.58,0:11:28.28,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I'm still in this miserable state.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:28.38,0:11:31.08,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Well, a vacation once in a\Nwhile isn't such a bad thing...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:31.18,0:11:33.08,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,or so I'd like to say,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:33.18,0:11:34.08,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,but I need to ask you a favour.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:34.18,0:11:35.38,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,What is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:35.48,0:11:37.58,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I'll help with anything,\Nas long as I'm able to do it.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:38.48,0:11:41.28,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I've sent over one Tachikoma unit.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:41.98,0:11:46.98,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Half of the plutonium we retrieved\Nfrom the radio tower is in its pod.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:47.08,0:11:49.68,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Take that and go to Spring-8.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:49.78,0:11:52.28,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I see, so that's how it is.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:52.88,0:11:54.78,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I don't mind.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:54.88,0:11:55.98,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,but what are you guys going to do?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:57.08,0:12:00.38,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,We're going to take the\Nremaining plutonium to Dejima.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:00.48,0:12:01.88,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,To Dejima?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:01.98,0:12:04.58,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Thought up another foolish plan, have you?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:05.28,0:12:06.48,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,What about Togusa?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:06.48,0:12:08.58,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,He's with the Chief at the\NPrime Minister's office.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:08.68,0:12:09.48,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:09.58,0:12:12.68,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Major, I'm sorry I can't join you guys.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:12.78,0:12:14.48,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Be careful.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:14.58,0:12:17.88,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,You don't know what will happen\Nif they begin an air raid.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:17.98,0:12:19.08,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:19.78,0:12:21.38,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,You be careful too.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:24.22,0:12:25.72,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,You can count on me.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:25.82,0:12:27.12,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I'm counting on you.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:27.22,0:12:28.89,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,You'll see us on the news
Dialogue: 0,0:12:28.92,0:12:31.72,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,when we hand the plutonium\Nover to the UN inspection team.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:37.53,0:12:40.33,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Don't die, Major.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:42.83,0:12:44.43,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Hey, Major.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:46.23,0:12:47.93,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Can I ask you something?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:48.03,0:12:49.03,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:50.23,0:12:54.13,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,When I talked to Gouda using\Nyour external memory...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:54.23,0:12:58.33,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I felt bad about doing it,\Nbut I looked into your memory about Kuze.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:58.43,0:12:59.13,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,And?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:59.93,0:13:02.63,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,It's not like I actually saw anything,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:02.73,0:13:05.43,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,but it seems like you have some\Nspecial feelings towards Kuze.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:06.43,0:13:09.13,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,What happened when you dived into his brain?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:11.93,0:13:14.43,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Nothing special happened.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:14.53,0:13:17.23,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,But when I touched his memories,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:17.33,0:13:20.13,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,it felt like he was someone I once\Nhad a close relationship with.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:20.63,0:13:22.93,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,A close relationship?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:23.03,0:13:24.03,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:24.63,0:13:27.09,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,But it happened a very long time ago.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:29.13,0:13:30.73,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,We're almost there.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:42.89,0:13:45.29,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Are they really going to attack?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:45.89,0:13:48.89,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,We're prepared to make a suicide bombing strike.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:49.69,0:13:52.29,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Comrade Kuze said not to do anything.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:53.19,0:13:55.39,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Make sure we don't act first.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:55.49,0:13:58.89,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Then international opinion will be on our side.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:58.99,0:14:02.19,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,We will win this fight without fighting.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:03.09,0:14:04.99,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Make sure you stay connected to Kuze's net.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:22.09,0:14:24.59,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,You're Kuze Hideo, aren't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:25.39,0:14:26.49,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,And you are?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:30.58,0:14:33.88,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I'd seen you once before overseas.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:34.88,0:14:35.88,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Is that so.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:36.98,0:14:44.68,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,You were surrounded by a crowd in Taiwan, but it\Nseems only a few in Dejima know what you look like.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:45.58,0:14:48.58,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,There are many who have cyberbrains here, so...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:48.68,0:14:50.18,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:50.98,0:14:55.28,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,So that's why your beliefs have been\Npropagated among the refugees...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:56.58,0:14:57.98,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Of course,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:58.08,0:15:04.38,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I believe it to be a divine feat that could only\Nhave been achieved with the mental fortitude
Dialogue: 0,0:15:04.48,0:15:06.88,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,to continually respond to queries\Nfrom three million people.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:07.88,0:15:08.88,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,However,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:08.98,0:15:10.68,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,there was a pitfall to that.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:11.28,0:15:13.08,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Pitfall?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:13.18,0:15:14.18,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:15.48,0:15:17.38,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Water flows to lower heights,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:17.48,0:15:20.18,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,and so does the human heart.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:22.85,0:15:26.45,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,When I returned to Dejima after\Npurging the thought virus,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:26.55,0:15:29.35,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,the refugees began to connect to me right away.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:30.15,0:15:31.75,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I valued their thoughts
Dialogue: 0,0:15:31.85,0:15:36.15,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,and made it my sole behavioural principle
Dialogue: 0,0:15:36.25,0:15:38.25,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,to help them fulfil their wishes.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:39.05,0:15:42.95,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,It wasn't too difficult to become their leader.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:44.55,0:15:47.25,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I put filters on the consciousness of others
Dialogue: 0,0:15:47.35,0:15:49.75,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,and made an effort to synchronise\Nthe consciousness of the refugees,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:49.85,0:15:53.25,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,who are ceaselessly connected to\Nmine, with my ideals.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:54.05,0:15:55.45,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,After the Great War,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:55.55,0:15:57.45,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I wandered through the Eurasian continent
Dialogue: 0,0:15:57.55,0:16:01.65,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,and sought the raison d'etre\Nof individuals in a system.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:02.25,0:16:03.35,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,In the process,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:03.85,0:16:05.05,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,the refugees taught me
Dialogue: 0,0:16:05.15,0:16:10.35,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,that humans only exist through\Nthe intervention of others.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:11.85,0:16:15.15,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,If you weigh your duties and your rights
Dialogue: 0,0:16:15.25,0:16:18.25,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,and first add weight to your rights,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:18.35,0:16:23.05,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,then you would not lose yourself\Neven if you were to obey social laws.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:26.45,0:16:27.15,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:31.52,0:16:36.52,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,That universal thought seemed very agreeable.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:37.42,0:16:38.52,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,However, even the refugees
Dialogue: 0,0:16:39.22,0:16:43.72,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,forget that and flow to lower heights
Dialogue: 0,0:16:43.82,0:16:47.32,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,once they learn of the upper echelons via the net,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:48.22,0:16:50.02,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,When they have power, they want to show it off,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:50.92,0:16:54.02,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,in the same way they'd like to\Ntry out a weapon if they had one.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:55.12,0:16:59.22,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Knowing that, why did you pull\Nthe situation along this far?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:59.32,0:17:04.92,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Did you really believe something as far-fetched\Nas a revolution could be accomplished that easily?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:05.52,0:17:06.62,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,No.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:06.72,0:17:10.72,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,However, the revolution I have in\Nmind lies further on in the future.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:12.22,0:17:15.12,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Right now, I believe that making\Npeople head towards the superstructure,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:15.22,0:17:18.72,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,the revolution's goal, is a preliminary step.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:18.82,0:17:20.32,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Superstructure?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:21.02,0:17:23.62,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Is that different from hierarchy?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:23.72,0:17:25.12,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Yes, it is different.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:26.12,0:17:28.92,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The network, which is about to envelop this world,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:29.02,0:17:31.12,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,has already turned into the infrastructure,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:31.22,0:17:35.32,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,it has fulfilled its original purpose\Nand is now something different.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:35.92,0:17:37.52,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,From there, it will achieve an existence
Dialogue: 0,0:17:37.62,0:17:39.82,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,that will exert a counteractive\Neffect on the infrastructure,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:39.92,0:17:43.42,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,from which it is inseparable,\Nbut which is nonetheless its foundation,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:43.52,0:17:45.62,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,and shift into a superstructure.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:57.16,0:18:00.86,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,That is my definition of a revolution.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:00.96,0:18:02.69,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I don't really understand,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:02.76,0:18:05.76,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,but is it possible to share\Nthat belief with the refugees?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:06.96,0:18:09.76,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Subconsciously, we should already be sharing it,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:09.86,0:18:11.36,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,but not yet in a concrete sense,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:13.66,0:18:18.36,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I gave up power in the past,\Nout of curiosity towards others.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:18.46,0:18:21.86,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,If you would allow this old man a word,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:21.96,0:18:25.56,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,you should prioritise the\Nreality over the ideal right now.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:25.66,0:18:28.66,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,You can still put a stop to this.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:00.22,0:19:00.82,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Tachikoma.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:00.92,0:19:02.72,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I'm going to dive into Kuze's\Ncyberbrain one more time.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:02.82,0:19:03.52,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Give me backup.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:04.92,0:19:06.12,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Is that going to be okay?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:06.62,0:19:08.82,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Connecting won't be a problem;
Dialogue: 0,0:19:08.92,0:19:12.12,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,whether he'll accept our message\Nis another story, though.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:23.11,0:19:25.91,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Oomura station just reported\Nthat a chopper took off,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:26.01,0:19:27.51,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,even though it was not scheduled for a mission.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:28.31,0:19:29.81,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,So they've been found.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:29.91,0:19:33.01,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,They're acting precisely like the scenario.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:33.11,0:19:36.11,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,What is the status on EP-3C deployment?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:36.21,0:19:39.81,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,It has already arrived above Dejima, sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:39.91,0:19:41.31,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Good.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:41.41,0:19:42.91,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Start there.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:43.01,0:19:45.11,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Jam all signals in Dejima
Dialogue: 0,0:19:45.21,0:19:47.41,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,and turn the refugees into stand alones.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:47.51,0:19:50.51,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The refugees will then begin\Ngoing out of control on their own.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:03.27,0:20:05.37,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The net is going to get disconnected.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:05.47,0:20:07.77,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,It seems transmissions in\NDejima are being disrupted.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:07.87,0:20:10.07,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Put the firewall array on standby.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:10.17,0:20:12.07,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Punch the message file through in one shot!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:12.17,0:20:13.47,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Roger!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:20.53,0:20:21.53,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:22.44,0:20:23.44,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,What's wrong?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:23.44,0:20:24.84,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,They'll come here?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:25.34,0:20:26.94,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,With the plutonium on top of that?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:27.84,0:20:29.34,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,What are you talking about?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:29.44,0:20:31.14,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The net has been disconnected.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:32.04,0:20:33.34,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The SDF must be jamming it.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:42.48,0:20:44.98,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,They intend to isolate the refugees.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:46.68,0:20:48.28,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The tanks are attacking!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:48.78,0:20:53.08,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,It seems someone in the government\Nthinks the same way I do.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:58.08,0:21:00.58,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I will go to the barricade on Oohashi bridge.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:00.68,0:21:02.78,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,There is a high probability\Nthat fighting will begin.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:03.98,0:21:06.08,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,People like you mustn't die.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:06.68,0:21:08.98,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,If you can, please escape from Dejima.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:09.68,0:21:11.98,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,You mustn't die, either.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:12.58,0:21:14.58,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,There must be something you can still do.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:15.38,0:21:16.88,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I hope so.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:25.42,0:21:25.92,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,How did it go?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:26.52,0:21:29.42,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The transmission finished a split\Nsecond before the disconnect!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:29.52,0:21:30.52,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Good.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:38.91,0:21:40.71,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Dammit, I'll get 'em!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:47.38,0:21:48.48,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I got him!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:50.28,0:21:51.48,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,He was shot!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:51.58,0:21:52.88,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Cover us!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:01.70,0:22:02.70,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Gunshots!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:02.80,0:22:03.60,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,is there combat?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:06.96,0:22:07.66,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Stop that!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:07.76,0:22:09.26,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Don't shoot! Stop!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:09.36,0:22:10.76,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,They have nukes!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:13.85,0:22:16.05,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Water flows to lower heights,
Dialogue: 0,0:22:16.15,0:22:19.45,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,and so does the human heart.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:19.61,0:22:22.81,Sign,,0,1450,755,,{\fs48}{\b1}Dejima - Oohashi Bridge{\b0}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:22.74,0:22:23.94,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,What the hell?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:24.04,0:22:25.64,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Seems the fighting's begun.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:30.52,0:22:32.22,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The tanks {\i1}are{\i} coming!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:32.32,0:22:33.82,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Destroy the bridge!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:10.56,0:23:12.86,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Finding out a galaxy
Dialogue: 0,0:23:12.91,0:23:16.76,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,of planets and stars within me.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:17.01,0:23:19.16,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Listening to each of them
Dialogue: 0,0:23:19.36,0:23:23.16,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,singing the same silent melody.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:23.16,0:23:27.16,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I've never seen such beauty
Dialogue: 0,0:23:27.66,0:23:30.39,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,in possibility...
Dialogue: 0,0:23:30.96,0:23:34.73,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,No smack of doubt or fear.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:35.16,0:23:36.66,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,(Wake up)
Dialogue: 0,0:23:36.76,0:23:38.76,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I hear a voice.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:37.59,0:23:40.99,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,(And show the light)
Dialogue: 0,0:23:39.35,0:23:41.86,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,hear a voice calling out to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:41.87,0:23:43.04,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,(Wake up)
Dialogue: 0,0:23:43.53,0:23:45.33,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I see inside
Dialogue: 0,0:23:44.13,0:23:48.33,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,(the time is right)
Dialogue: 0,0:23:46.16,0:23:49.46,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,see the light now ever holding me.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:49.56,0:23:50.72,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,All the truth,
Dialogue: 0,0:23:51.11,0:23:53.11,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,All I need,
Dialogue: 0,0:23:51.10,0:23:51.70,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,(All the truth)
Dialogue: 0,0:23:52.98,0:23:56.28,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,to make all this reality.
